AC families:

  - AC.QSURF.1 — onboarding_mode flag toggles enforcement.
    With onboarding_mode=True, surface_next_questions_batch()
    returns exactly 1 question per call regardless of n or
    max_questions_per_turn. With onboarding_mode=False, returns
    up to min(n, max_questions_per_turn, len(queue)).
  - AC.QSURF.2 — non-onboarding-mode permits batched surfacing.
    With max_questions_per_turn=3 + n=3, batch returns 3; queue
    advances by 3; audit-log records 3 surface_question entries
    with FIFO order preserved; per-batch queue_position fields.
  - AC.QSURF.3 — onboarding hard test. 5 simulated turns × 1
    question per turn × 5 enqueued questions, structurally
    deterministic (assertion `len(returned) == 1` per turn — never
    randomly passes). Repeated-run determinism verified.
  - AC.QSURF.4 — audit-log records each surfacing AND each
    response with full provenance. record_response audit entry
    carries: schema_version, event_kind=record_response,
    timestamp, pm_handle, response_text, surfaced_audit_path
    (relative to PM dir), surfaced_question_text, responded_at.
    NNNN counter shared across event_kinds within (pm-name, UTC
    date). Linkage round-trippable.
  - AC.QSURF.5 — require_owner_response=True blocks subsequent
    surfacings via surface_next_questions_batch (NOT via
    surface_next_question — Cycle 2 contract preserved per plan
    §5 Surface #8 fallback). PendingResponseError carries
    pending_question + surfaced_audit_path. With
    require_owner_response=False, no blocking. Blocking does NOT
    partial-surface.
  - AC.QSURF.6 — record_response API. Returns RecordedResponse;
    writes audit entry; clears pending_response_for; idempotent
    on duplicate (returns prior recorded response without dup
    write); rejects empty text; rejects missing path; rejects
    wrong event_kind on link; accepts relative path.
  - AC.QSURF.7 — PM-mediated dispatches log per audit-trail floor
    (SOC-2 — Eric synthesis Decision P alignment). Every
    surfacing + every response writes one audit entry. Every
    entry carries pm_handle + ISO 8601 timezone-aware timestamp
    + schema_version=1.
  - AC.QSURF.8 — composition with audit-block-on-telegram SKILL.
    SurfacedQuestion + RecordedResponse expose
    `is_audit_block_trigger` property (returns True at Cycle 4
    unconditionally; forward-compat extension point). design.md
    §12 cross-references the SKILL by exact path
    (`plugins/loam-skills/skills/audit-block-on-telegram/`) and
    names the "decision was made" trigger condition. Test
    verifies (a) property exposes True on both classes,
    (b) design-note carries path + trigger string, (c) SKILL.md
    actually exists at named path AND contains trigger string,
    (d) property docstrings reference both SKILL name +
    trigger string.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Blocking enforcement on `surface_next_questions_batch` only;
    `surface_next_question` (Cycle 2 API) preserved verbatim per
    plan §5 Surface #8 fallback. The Cycle 2 contract is
    load-bearing — 64 Cycle 2 tests pass unchanged after Cycle 4
    runtime extension. The structural one-question-at-a-time
    discipline lives on the batch API; the single-question API
    remains the "low-discipline" surface.
  - `pending_response_for` field added to state.yaml schema
    (vs separate file). Backward-compat: Cycle 2 state.yaml
    loads as `pending_response_for=None`.
  - record_response audit entry stores `surfaced_audit_path` as
    a path RELATIVE to PM dir (portable if workspace is moved).
  - Idempotency on duplicate record_response: scan audit-log/ for
    existing record_response entry whose surfaced_audit_path
    matches; on hit, return prior RecordedResponse without
    writing a duplicate entry (audit-log is the source of truth).
  - `is_audit_block_trigger` is a `@property` (not always-True
    field) on both event classes. Forward-compat: future cycles
    may gate on event metadata; the property mechanism is the
    extension point.
  - Batch with require_owner_response=True surfaces ONE question
    then stops (subsequent surfacings would be blocked anyway);
    next call raises PendingResponseError. Predictable shape;
    no partial state.
  - PendingResponseError carries pending_question +
    surfaced_audit_path on the exception body so the caller can
    re-prompt the user without a second loader call.
  - Tests = 8 NEW files (one per AC.QSURF.{1..8}); 50 new tests;
    all pass; cumulative per-project-pm count 114 tests
    (64 Cycle 2 + 50 Cycle 4) all green.
  - Public API surface re-exported via `__init__.py` for
    `from loam.per_project_pm import RecordedResponse,
    PendingResponseError`.

